    body: "<!-- TEMPLATE — requires attorney review before launch -->\n\n# Acceptable Use & Messaging Policy\n\nThis policy governs your use of {{LEGAL_ENTITY_NAME}}'s messaging features and mirrors carrier and CTIA requirements. Violation may result in immediate suspension.\n\n## 1. Consent Is Required\n\nYou must have prior express consent to message every recipient before importing or contacting them. **Purchased or scraped lists are prohibited.** You must be able to produce proof of consent on request.\n\n## 2. Prohibited Content (SHAFT)\n\nMessages must not contain content relating to Sex, Hate, Alcohol, Firearms, or Tobacco, nor any unlawful, deceptive, or high-risk financial content prohibited by carriers.\n\n## 3. Mandatory STOP / HELP Handling\n\n- **STOP** (and equivalents) immediately and permanently adds the number to the suppression list; no further messages may be sent to it.\n- **HELP** returns program information and support contact.\n\nThese behaviors are enforced by the platform server-side and may not be disabled.\n\n## 4. Quiet Hours\n\nMessages are only sent between 8:00 AM and 9:00 PM in the recipient's local time zone. Messages scheduled outside that window are automatically deferred.\n\n## 5. No Spam / Volume Abuse\n\nDo not send unsolicited bulk messages, evade opt-outs, or otherwise abuse the platform. Excessive complaints or opt-out rates may trigger review and suspension.\n\n## 6. Enforcement\n\nWe may suspend or terminate accounts that violate this policy. Repeated or egregious violations result in permanent termination. Questions: {{SUPPORT_EMAIL}}\n",
