    body: "<!-- TEMPLATE — requires attorney review before launch -->\n\n# Terms of Service\n\nThese Terms of Service (\"Terms\") govern your access to and use of the software platform operated by {{LEGAL_ENTITY_NAME}}, a company organized under the laws of {{LEGAL_ENTITY_STATE}} (\"Company,\" \"we,\" \"us\"). By creating an account or using the platform, you agree to these Terms.\n\n## 1. The Platform Is a Tool — Not a Brokerage\n\nThe platform is a software tool that helps you manage outreach, conversations, and contracts for real estate transactions. **The Company is not a licensed real estate brokerage, agent, or broker.** We do not:\n\n- Buy, sell, list, or represent any real property\n- Represent any party in a real estate transaction\n- Provide offers, counteroffers, or negotiate on your behalf\n- Hold earnest money, deposits, or any funds related to transactions\n- Guarantee the validity, enforceability, or legality of any contract\n\n**You — not the Company — are the sender of every message transmitted through the platform.** You are solely responsible for all activity conducted through your account.\n\n## 2. User Responsibilities and Compliance\n\nYou acknowledge and agree that:\n\n### 2.1 Messaging Compliance\n\nYou are solely responsible for obtaining all legally required consent before contacting anyone, and for complying with:\n\n- The Telephone Consumer Protection Act (TCPA)\n- The CAN-SPAM Act\n- CTIA messaging guidelines\n- State-specific telemarketing and do-not-call laws\n- All applicable federal, state, and local laws\n\n### 2.2 Real Estate Compliance\n\nYou are responsible for understanding and complying with:\n\n- State and local real estate licensing requirements\n- Wholesaling and assignment regulations in your jurisdiction\n- Disclosure requirements for property transactions\n- Fair Housing Act requirements\n- State-specific contract requirements and cooling-off periods\n- Any applicable recording or registration requirements\n\n### 2.3 Documentation and Record-Keeping\n\nYou must maintain accurate records of:\n\n- Consent documentation for all contacts\n- All contracts, amendments, and addenda\n- Communication logs as required by law\n- Any required disclosures provided to parties\n\n## 3. No Legal, Financial, or Real Estate Advice\n\n**The Company does not provide legal, financial, tax, real estate brokerage, or investment advice.** \n\n- Contract templates provided are examples only and may not comply with your jurisdiction's requirements\n- You should have all contracts reviewed by a licensed attorney before use\n- Property valuations, if any, are estimates only and should not be relied upon for transaction decisions\n- The platform does not verify or guarantee the accuracy of any property data\n\n**Always consult licensed professionals** (attorneys, real estate agents, accountants, title companies) before entering into any transaction.\n\n## 4. No Earnings Guarantee\n\nResults depend on market conditions, your skill, effort, capital, and local regulations. The Company makes no representation or guarantee regarding:\n\n- Deals closed or revenue generated\n- Return on investment\n- Accuracy of property valuations\n- Responsiveness of contacts\n- Market conditions or property values\n\nNothing in the platform constitutes a promise, projection, or guarantee of earnings. Past performance by other users does not guarantee future results.\n\n## 5. Contract Templates Disclaimer\n\nAny contract templates, forms, or documents provided through the platform:\n\n- Are provided as examples and starting points only\n- May not comply with laws in your jurisdiction\n- May require modification for your specific transaction\n- Are not a substitute for documents prepared by a licensed attorney\n- May become outdated as laws change\n\n**You are solely responsible for ensuring any contract you use is valid, enforceable, and compliant with applicable law.** The Company makes no warranty regarding the legal sufficiency of any template.\n\n## 6. Accounts and Acceptable Use\n\nYou must provide accurate registration information and keep your credentials secure. Your use of the messaging features is additionally governed by our Acceptable Use & Messaging Policy, which is incorporated into these Terms by reference. You agree not to:\n\n- Use the platform for any unlawful purpose\n- Send messages to contacts without proper consent\n- Violate any person's privacy or intellectual property rights\n- Transmit malware, spam, or deceptive content\n- Circumvent or disable any security features\n- Use the platform in any way that could damage our reputation or services\n\n## 7. Indemnification\n\nYou agree to indemnify, defend, and hold harmless the Company and its officers, directors, employees, agents, and affiliates from any and all claims, losses, damages, liabilities, costs, and expenses (including reasonable attorneys' fees) arising out of or related to:\n\n- Your use of the platform\n- Your messages, campaigns, and communications\n- Your contracts, transactions, and business dealings\n- Your violation of any law, regulation, or these Terms\n- Your infringement of any third-party rights\n- Any complaint, claim, or legal action brought by a recipient of your messages\n\n## 8. Limitation of Liability\n\n**THE PLATFORM IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\" WITHOUT WARRANTIES OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED.** The Company disclaims all warranties, including implied warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and non-infringement.\n\nTO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW:\n\n- The Company is not liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages\n- The Company is not liable for lost profits, revenue, data, or business opportunities\n- The Company is not liable for any damages arising from your transactions with third parties\n- The Company's total liability is limited to the amount you paid to the Company in the twelve (12) months preceding the claim\n\nSome jurisdictions do not allow certain warranty disclaimers or liability limitations, so some of the above may not apply to you.\n\n## 9. Dispute Resolution\n\n### 9.1 Governing Law\n\nThese Terms are governed by the laws of {{LEGAL_ENTITY_STATE}}, without regard to conflict of law principles.\n\n### 9.2 Arbitration Agreement\n\n[FOR ATTORNEY REVIEW — arbitration clause, class action waiver, and venue/jurisdiction provisions to be finalized by counsel licensed in {{LEGAL_ENTITY_STATE}}.]\n\n### 9.3 Time Limitation\n\nAny claim arising under these Terms must be brought within one (1) year after the cause of action arises, or the claim is permanently barred.\n\n## 10. Termination\n\nWe may suspend or terminate your access immediately and without notice for:\n\n- Violation of these Terms or the Acceptable Use Policy\n- Fraudulent, abusive, or illegal activity\n- Non-payment of fees\n- Requests from law enforcement or government agencies\n- Extended periods of inactivity\n\nYou may cancel your account at any time as described in the Refund & Billing Policy. Upon termination:\n\n- Your license to use the platform ends immediately\n- You remain liable for any unpaid fees\n- Provisions that by their nature should survive termination will survive\n\n## 11. Changes to Terms\n\nWe may modify these Terms at any time by posting the revised version and updating the effective date. Material changes will be communicated via email or in-app notification. Your continued use after changes constitutes acceptance of the modified Terms.\n\n## 12. Severability\n\nIf any provision of these Terms is found unenforceable, the remaining provisions will continue in full force and effect.\n\n## 13. Entire Agreement\n\nThese Terms, together with the Privacy Policy, Acceptable Use Policy, and other policies referenced herein, constitute the entire agreement between you and the Company regarding your use of the platform.\n\n## 14. Contact\n\nQuestions about these Terms: {{SUPPORT_EMAIL}}\n",
